# T014: `npm pack` exclusions (packaging only — no src/oracle change).
# NOTE (npm rule, verified this round): files listed in package.json
# `files` CANNOT be excluded by .npmignore, so the allowlist itself
# omits the generated paths — `demo` is listed as its three shippable
# entries (claimed-map.json, README.md, repo/) and `oracle` as
# oracle/python/oracle.py, leaving out demo/out/ and the compiled
# oracle .pyc. This file is defense-in-depth for anything packed by
# default (no `files` entry): if the `files` field is ever removed,
# these exclusions apply again. Do NOT blanket-exclude `__pycache__/` —
# the regression fixtures under tests/fixtures/regression/ deliberately
# contain `__pycache__` dirs holding source files
# (e.g. go-pycache/repo/__pycache__/x.go); only compiled bytecode is junk.
demo/out/
.tmp/
*.pyc
